Presets are names 'ley tune' accepts in place of a frequency. Each one is a
fixed frequency and mode; ley does not probe or scan for the best channel
(that is 'ley scan', see ley help roadmap). Names are case-insensitive.

  noaa1     162.550 MHz  nfm  NOAA weather WX1                                also: noaa, wx1, weather
  noaa2     162.400 MHz  nfm  NOAA weather WX2                                also: wx2
  noaa3     162.475 MHz  nfm  NOAA weather WX3                                also: wx3
  noaa4     162.425 MHz  nfm  NOAA weather WX4                                also: wx4
  noaa5     162.450 MHz  nfm  NOAA weather WX5                                also: wx5
  noaa6     162.500 MHz  nfm  NOAA weather WX6                                also: wx6
  noaa7     162.525 MHz  nfm  NOAA weather WX7                                also: wx7
  calling   146.520 MHz  nfm  2 m amateur national simplex calling frequency  also: 2m-calling, simplex
  marine16  156.800 MHz  nfm  marine VHF channel 16, distress and calling     also: marine
  guard     121.500 MHz  am   aviation emergency guard frequency              also: aircraft-guard, 121.5
  ch1       462.562 MHz  nfm  GMRS/FRS channel 1, 462.5625 MHz                
  ch2       462.587 MHz  nfm  GMRS/FRS channel 2, 462.5875 MHz                
  ch3       462.613 MHz  nfm  GMRS/FRS channel 3, 462.6125 MHz                
  ch4       462.637 MHz  nfm  GMRS/FRS channel 4, 462.6375 MHz                
  ch5       462.663 MHz  nfm  GMRS/FRS channel 5, 462.6625 MHz                
  ch6       462.688 MHz  nfm  GMRS/FRS channel 6, 462.6875 MHz                
  ch7       462.712 MHz  nfm  GMRS/FRS channel 7, 462.7125 MHz                
  ch8       467.562 MHz  nfm  GMRS/FRS channel 8, 467.5625 MHz                
  ch9       467.587 MHz  nfm  GMRS/FRS channel 9, 467.5875 MHz                
  ch10      467.613 MHz  nfm  GMRS/FRS channel 10, 467.6125 MHz               
  ch11      467.637 MHz  nfm  GMRS/FRS channel 11, 467.6375 MHz               
  ch12      467.663 MHz  nfm  GMRS/FRS channel 12, 467.6625 MHz               
  ch13      467.688 MHz  nfm  GMRS/FRS channel 13, 467.6875 MHz               
  ch14      467.712 MHz  nfm  GMRS/FRS channel 14, 467.7125 MHz               
  ch15      462.550 MHz  nfm  GMRS channel 15, 462.550 MHz                    also: rpt1, 15rp, ch23
  ch16      462.575 MHz  nfm  GMRS channel 16, 462.575 MHz                    also: rpt2, 16rp, ch24
  ch17      462.600 MHz  nfm  GMRS channel 17, 462.600 MHz                    also: rpt3, 17rp, ch25
  ch18      462.625 MHz  nfm  GMRS channel 18, 462.625 MHz                    also: rpt4, 18rp, ch26
  ch19      462.650 MHz  nfm  GMRS channel 19, 462.650 MHz                    also: rpt5, 19rp, ch27
  ch20      462.675 MHz  nfm  GMRS channel 20, 462.675 MHz                    also: rpt6, 20rp, ch28
  ch21      462.700 MHz  nfm  GMRS channel 21, 462.700 MHz                    also: rpt7, 21rp, ch29
  ch22      462.725 MHz  nfm  GMRS channel 22, 462.725 MHz                    also: rpt8, 22rp, ch30

Bands ley recognises. Without --mode, tune uses the band's mode and
bandwidth; outside every band it uses NFM and says "no band recognised".
usb/lsb means the sideband follows the amateur convention: USB at and above
10 MHz, LSB below (ley help modes).

  AM broadcast          530.000 kHz to 1.700 MHz    am       10 kHz    medium-wave broadcast stations
  160 m amateur         1.800 MHz to 2.000 MHz      usb/lsb  2.8 kHz   amateur radio, LSB voice
  80 m amateur          3.500 MHz to 4.000 MHz      usb/lsb  2.8 kHz   amateur radio, LSB voice
  40 m amateur          7.000 MHz to 7.300 MHz      usb/lsb  2.8 kHz   amateur radio, LSB voice
  20 m amateur          14.000 MHz to 14.350 MHz    usb/lsb  2.8 kHz   amateur radio, USB voice
  15 m amateur          21.000 MHz to 21.450 MHz    usb/lsb  2.8 kHz   amateur radio, USB voice
  CB                    26.965 MHz to 27.405 MHz    am       10 kHz    citizens band, channel 1 to 40
  10 m amateur          28.000 MHz to 29.700 MHz    usb/lsb  2.8 kHz   amateur radio, USB voice
  FM broadcast          87.500 MHz to 108.000 MHz   wfm      200 kHz   wideband FM radio stations
  airband               118.000 MHz to 137.000 MHz  am       10 kHz    aircraft and towers, AM voice
  2 m amateur           144.000 MHz to 148.000 MHz  nfm      12.5 kHz  amateur radio, FM voice and repeaters
  marine VHF            156.000 MHz to 162.025 MHz  nfm      12.5 kHz  ship and coast stations; channel 16 is 156.800
  NOAA weather          162.400 MHz to 162.550 MHz  nfm      12.5 kHz  continuous weather broadcasts, WX1 to WX7
  70 cm amateur         420.000 MHz to 450.000 MHz  nfm      12.5 kHz  amateur radio, FM voice and repeaters
  GMRS                  462.500 MHz to 462.750 MHz  nfm      20 kHz    GMRS/FRS 462 MHz channels: repeater outputs and simplex -- scan here to find a repeater's transmit
  GMRS repeater inputs  467.500 MHz to 467.750 MHz  nfm      20 kHz    GMRS repeater inputs, the uplink a radio transmits to a repeater

  ley tune noaa                noaa is an alias of noaa1, 162.550 MHz
  ley tune calling             146.520 MHz, 2 m simplex calling
  ley tune guard               121.500 MHz, AM
